BT /F2 14 Tf .2 .25 .2 rg 1 0 0 1 55 658 Tm (2 Scaled Dot-Product Attention) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf .2 .25 .2 rg 1 0 0 1 55 629 Tm (Each token is mapped to a query, a key, and a value, conventionally written as Q, K, and V.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf .2 .25 .2 rg 1 0 0 1 55 599 Tm (The dot product between a query and a key measures their compatibility.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf .2 .25 .2 rg 1 0 0 1 55 569 Tm (Dividing the scores by the square root of the key dimension helps keep their magnitude) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf .2 .25 .2 rg 1 0 0 1 55 552 Tm (manageable.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf .2 .25 .2 rg 1 0 0 1 55 522 Tm (A softmax converts these scores into nonnegative weights that sum to one.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf .2 .25 .2 rg 1 0 0 1 55 492 Tm (The weighted sum of values produces a context-sensitive representation for each query.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf .2 .25 .2 rg 1 0 0 1 55 462 Tm (Figure 1 illustrates the flow from queries and keys to attention weights and the final output.) Tj ET
