BT /F2 14 Tf .2 .25 .2 rg 1 0 0 1 55 658 Tm (3 Multi-Head Attention) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf .2 .25 .2 rg 1 0 0 1 55 629 Tm (Multiple attention heads apply different learned projections to the same input.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf .2 .25 .2 rg 1 0 0 1 55 599 Tm (This allows the model to represent several kinds of relationships at the same time.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf .2 .25 .2 rg 1 0 0 1 55 569 Tm (The outputs of the heads are concatenated and passed through a final linear projection.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf .2 .25 .2 rg 1 0 0 1 55 539 Tm (Positional information is also needed because attention alone does not specify the order of) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf .2 .25 .2 rg 1 0 0 1 55 522 Tm (the tokens.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf .2 .25 .2 rg 1 0 0 1 55 492 Tm (In practice, interpreting attention weights requires care: they describe one part of the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf .2 .25 .2 rg 1 0 0 1 55 475 Tm (computation rather than a complete explanation of the prediction.) Tj ET
BT /F3 8 Tf .6 .65 .55 rg 1 0 0 1 55 18 Tm (3 / 3   -   Educational sample, not a research publication) Tj ET
endstream
